 Gang'd F2 \u2192 suggests no one wants it.\n\nThus, **F2 is safe to discard**.\n\nCompare to others:\n- W3: I have two, unshown=2 \u2192 two others still in play \u2192 dangerous\n- J3: I have one, unshown=2 \u2192 two others \u2192 dragons are always risky\n- T5: used by across player \u2192 probably safe, but unshown=2 \u2192 risk remains\n- F4: I have one, unshown=3 \u2192 very dangerous (only one played)\n- B3: I have one, unshown=1 \u2192 previous player used two in chows \u2192 likely done \u2192 low risk\n- B7: I have one, unshown=1 \u2192 both I and next player used B7 in [B6,B7,B8] \u2192 so at least two used \u2192 possibly third too \u2192 but still one unshown \u2192 risk\n\nBest choice: **Play F2** \u2014 completely safe, no point in keeping it (I don't have a pair, can't form pung), and it's not useful for any major pattern.\n\nAnswer: Play F2"}
